WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:05.280
Avengers: Infinity War features more super-characters
than you can shake a cosmically-powered stick

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.280
at.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.550
Most of them you know, and many of them have
had their own movies already.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:13.089
Even the Guardians of the Galaxy crew is pretty
familiar at this point, but some of the supporting

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:14.860
characters remain a little obscure.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.680
For instance: What's the deal with Nebula,
the bald, blue-skinned cyborg played by Karen

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.680
Gillan?

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.100
How is her comics incarnation different from
her character in the MCU?

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.360
Let's explore.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.380
Thanos' granddaughter?

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.690
When Nebula first appeared in Avengers #257,
Thanos wasn't even around.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:35.821
He'd been turned to stone years earlier, and
although he wasn't technically dead, he was

00:00:35.821 --> 00:00:37.300
just as out of the picture.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.100
One of the first actions Nebula took in those
comics was to claim Thanos' former headquarters,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.050
the Sanctuary II, for her own.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:48.601
When Starfox, Thanos' brother, claimed it
as his familial right, Nebula made the claim

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:54.399
that would come to define her: the space station
was rightfully hers, because Thanos was her

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:55.399
grandfather.

00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:56.820
Old look

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.430
In her early appearances, Nebula looked very
different from the bald cyborg she would eventually

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.430
become.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:06.830
She was a fully organic humanoid alien with
gauntlets that enabled her to fire destructive

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.440
beams from her wrists.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.750
She had long bluish-black hair that rose up
in big curls on the sides in one of those

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.860
hairstyles that's only possible in comics.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.530
Nebula belongs to a race called the Luphomoids.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.909
There are only a few of them left in the galaxy,
because Galactus ate the planet of Luphom

00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:25.860
and only those Luphomoids who were off-planet
survived.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:30.450
Other Luphomoids like Zorr, a villain who
first appeared in Nova #1, were desperate

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.070
to find a new home world for their people.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.760
Nebula never seemed interested in that.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.840
Being a space pirate and the leader of a fleet
of mercenaries seemed to be her truest calling.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.979
No love from "grandpa"

00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:46.070
Whether Nebula was being honest about her
relation to Thanos was never particularly

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.900
relevant as long as he wasn't actually around.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.759
Being a pirate and mercenary gave her plenty
to do in the universe-hopping Marvel Comics

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:53.810
of the 1980s.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:58.970
Of course, as all classic villains eventually
will, Thanos returned to life, resurrected

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.680
by Death herself.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.610
In Silver Surfer #38, he met the woman who
claimed to be his granddaughter.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.810
He was not impressed, and claimed never to
have fathered children.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.910
It was probably meant to be the truth at the
time but became a lie in light of later stories

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.700
... because comics are very complicated.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:20.060
Declaring Nebula's lies "unforgivable," Thanos
set her on fire with beams from his eyes.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:24.730
He meant to kill her, but crew members on
the Sanctuary II saved her life … in a manner

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:25.730
of speaking.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:29.430
When Thanos rediscovered Nebula after their
first meeting, she had been burned beyond

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:33.430
recognition, profoundly brain damaged, and
about to expire for real.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:38.150
By this time, Thanos had assembled the Infinity
Gems into the Infinity Gauntlet, giving himself

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.450
vast and godlike powers.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:45.220
He used those powers to stop Nebula from croaking
— without actually healing her.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:50.599
She existed as a shambling, nearly mindless,
charred zombie of a creature.

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:51.720
Thanos' downfall

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:56.700
A confrontation with the cosmic being known
as Eternity led to Thanos leaving his body

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.640
unattended while his consciousness dealt with
larger cosmic matters.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.610
This gave Nebula, who had been repeatedly
described as "nearly mindless," the opportunity

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:09.390
to grab the Infinity Gauntlet off of his hand
and claim its power for herself, immediately

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.420
restoring her body and mind in the process.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:16.170
She didn't keep the gauntlet for long, but
she enabled the defeat of Thanos, and was

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.879
restored from her zombie-like state in the
process.

00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:21.599
Bald is beautiful

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:25.560
After the events of The Infinity Gauntlet,
Nebula's physical form was restored, but her

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.200
brain was still damaged.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.560
Her longtime first mate, Geatar, freed her
from imprisonment and took her to a rogue

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.069
space surgeon who promised to restore her
faculties.

00:03:34.069 --> 00:03:39.700
When the fully restored Nebula was finally
unveiled in Silver Surfer #72, she'd become

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:45.030
a bald cyborg who should look very familiar
to Marvel Cinematic Universe fans.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:49.630
Finally back to her mental and physical peak,
and even beyond it, thanks to her cybernetic

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:53.849
implants, Nebula returned to the life of a
space pirate.

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:55.870
Amazing Graces

00:03:55.870 --> 00:04:01.599
In Annihilation: Ronan, one of the miniseries
that was part of Marvel's larger 2006 Annihilation

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:06.209
event, Nebula was reintroduced as a member
of a team of interstellar women warriors known

00:04:06.209 --> 00:04:07.209
as the Graces.

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:11.560
The leader of the Graces turned out to be
a woman with an even stronger connection to

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.599
Thanos than Nebula herself ever had: Gamora.

00:04:14.599 --> 00:04:19.160
Whereas Nebula only ever claimed to be the
granddaughter of Thanos, a claim never proven,

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.680
Gamora was actually raised by him.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:26.059
When Nicole Perlman and James Gunn were writing
Guardians of the Galaxy for the screen, and

00:04:26.059 --> 00:04:31.330
figuring out how to translate all the complex
mythology around Thanos to the cinematic universe,

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:35.610
a story emerged that was simpler and more
powerful than anything Nebula and Gamora had

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.089
dealt with in the comics: a story about sisters.

00:04:39.089 --> 00:04:40.779
MCU Update

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:46.330
The Nebula of the Guardians of the Galaxy
movies is, like Gamora, an adopted daughter

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.330
of Thanos.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:52.210
Unlike the fully organic Gamora, Nebula has
been enhanced with extremely visible cybernetics,

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.710
leaving her a mix of woman and machine who
suffers doubts about her own selfhood.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:01.600
Her self-doubt, combined with her close relationship
with Gamora, enables Nebula to turn against

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:05.439
Thanos and become a sympathetic character
and a grudging ally to the heroes.

00:05:05.439 --> 00:05:09.439
She refuses to join the Guardians of the Galaxy,
but by the end of their second movie, she's

00:05:09.439 --> 00:05:10.689
no longer the group's enemy.

00:05:10.689 --> 00:05:14.149
In fact, her new stated mission is to destroy
Thanos herself ...

00:05:14.149 --> 00:05:17.460
"I will help them by killing Thanos"

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.499
… setting up her appearances in Avengers:
Infinity War and its as-yet-untitled sequel.

00:05:21.499 --> 00:05:23.719
